    "body": "I'd prefer something simpler, more similiar to the old solution like this here. I am not sure how zero-cost closures are:\r\n```rust\r\n    let config = [\r\n        utils::read_file(context.get_env(\"PWD\").unwrap() + \"/clouds.yaml\"),\r\n        utils::read_file(dirs_next::home_dir()?.join(\".config/openstack/clouds.yaml\")),\r\n        utils::read_file(\"/etc/openstack/clouds.yaml\"),\r\n    ];\r\n    let clouds =\r\n        YamlLoader::load_from_str(&config.iter().find_map(|i| i.as_ref().ok()).unwrap()).ok()?;\r\n```\r\nIf you want to avoid reading all the files maybe just put the filenames into the array instead of closures. I feel like closures would overcomplicate this function:\r\n```rust\r\n    let config = [\r\n        context.get_env(\"PWD\").unwrap() + \"/clouds.yaml\",\r\n        dirs_next::home_dir()?.join(\".config/openstack/clouds.yaml\"),\r\n        \"/etc/openstack/clouds.yaml\",\r\n    ];\r\n````\r\nBut I like the way you simplified the function futher down.",
