    "body": "Indeed, I could avoid the closures and just use plain function pointers instead, which avoids one more indirection.\r\nHowever, I think the strings shouldn't be constructed up front, since some of the operations can fail, like `home_dir` returning `None`. In this case the function should not return, but instead try the other files it can, in order.",
